{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/441385-a-mummy-s-appearance","id":441385,"title":"A Mummy's Appearance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-14T09:07:49-07:00","id":441385,"title":"A Mummy's Appearance","content":"I have a question about mummies appearance. The core book states that a fresh awakened mummy is just like any mummy should be. So as player I'm going to put myself in the shoes of a dry corpse covered in bandages which have no chance to conceal his true nature? Then how a mummy can walk among humans? Someone asked me to try Mummy The Curse, but honestly play as a walking dry corpse is not something that excites me, and it's a pity because I really like it's game plot. Please, tell me if I'm misunderstanding or missing something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 03-14-2015, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:15:17-07:00","id":441404,"title":"","content":"Looking like a dry corpse is only temporary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:15:55-07:00","id":441406,"title":"","content":"More to the point, once you drop to Sekhem 8, your appearance becomes human-like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:19:43-07:00","id":441407,"title":"","content":"And that will take a couple of days, tops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:27:53-07:00","id":441450,"title":"","content":"It's a relief, the game plot is really nice but if the sekhem loses two points in two days... It means that an Arisen is able to stay alive only for 10 days?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:31:53-07:00","id":441452,"title":"","content":"No, the rate at which Sekhem declines radically slows the lower your rating gets. It's hard to be godlike. The world rejects and snuffs out your power. The weaker you become, the more you &quot;fit in&quot; as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:59:30-07:00","id":441523,"title":"","content":"For reference, it takes about as long to get to sekhem 5 as it does to then drop to 4. Which in both cases is around 20 days.<br /> <br /> Then it takes about 40 to drop to 3, then 60 to drop to 2, then 100 to drop to 1. And this will be extended because every time you would drop you roll your current sekhem and only drop if you succeed. If you fail, which is quite likely at low levels, you get a bit more time before you need to roll again. You can easily last years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-14-2015, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:18:09-07:00","id":441541,"title":"","content":"And this is before you start doing things that grant you resets on the clock for your current Sekhem as a result of pleasing the Judges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T17:02:30-07:00","id":477382,"title":"","content":"I see, thank you very much... but if I don't like to await 2 days to drop to level 8, how I can dispel sekhem quickly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T17:15:20-07:00","id":477385,"title":"","content":"You can sacrifice a dot of Sekhem to heal a point of Aggravated damage or refill your Willpower pool (unless you're Deceived). Gift of the Golden Ankh Tier 3 lets you sacrifice a dot of Sekhem to return a mortal to life within a few minutes of their death. If you don't have a reason to sacrifice Sekhem, I'd allow Arisen to forfeit their Sekhem in exchange for nothing if they're already at full health and Willpower, although it isn't much of an inconvenience to just spend Willpower on something and then refresh your pool with Sekhem.<br /> <br /> I should also note that the alternative scale involved uses scenes rather than days. If your Storyteller so chooses, you can easily find yourself at Sekhem 8 after three scenes, which can be pretty fast depending on your play style.<br /> <br /> All that said, you do miss out on a little of the experience if you never find out how awe-inspiring it is to be Sekhem 10. Part of the old age metaphor at Mummy's heart is remembering how strong you once were, and it's harder to do it if you never had a chance to revel in the heights of your power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}